{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/tokens/clax.tokens.json","issuer":"urn:lobby:seat:work-clax-design-tokens-stint","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T19:36:20.658491Z","id":"854236251232b7244bce71af9c8a281b9510b2908890895c7b82dfbfd711e662","body":{"detail":"Under forced-colors: active the overlay's --scrim and --shadow are Canvas, so a scrim behind a dialog hides the page completely rather than dimming it. Browsers force most author backgrounds under forced colours anyway; checking the overlay's dialog in Windows High Contrast (or Chrome's forced-colors emulation) would settle whether a transparent scrim reads better.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":307},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"8c3e4bcad693887f73ab1c9664edbdb5803ad143d04505dd1fdd5e2fe9c21bf1"},"summary":"theme.forced draws shadow and scrim as Canvas, an opaque colour","tags":["session:claude-code:4a38a244-bea1-40ba-afdf-38ccefe33974"]}}
